{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"and she sent and called Jacob\"</b> is that Jacob was in another place — he was not in the tent of his father and mother, for he was hiding because of Esau his brother, who was screaming against him, and he was ashamed before him or frightened:" "<b>\"Comforting himself regarding you, to kill you\"</b> — he comforts himself regarding the blessings through killing you; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 27:42). But its plain sense is \"comforting himself in you,\" and so too \"for you are chosen to be one of Jesse's sons\" (I Samuel 20:30), \"and he took hold for him\" (II Samuel 15:5), and many similar instances. Or its meaning is \"comforting himself concerning you,\" like \"for so the king had commanded concerning him\" (Esther 3:2). But Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 27:42) translated \"כמן לך\" — he lies in wait for you. And it appears from his opinion that the meaning of מתנחם לך is that he shows himself to you as comforted regarding the matter of the blessings, as though he is not aggrieved about them, while he is lying in wait so that you will not be on guard against him; and he translated the sense, not the literal word."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:06.371851525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}